# Documentation navigation gate

When adding or renaming a **navigable** public docs page (Guide / Architecture /
Reference / Developer / Agents / RFCs):

1. Add or update the matching file under `packages/docs/en/` (locale pair).
2. Register the route in `packages/docs/.vitepress/config.mts` sidebar (and `nav`
   if it is a top-level entry) for **both** `zh` and `en`.
3. If it is an RFC: also add a row to `developer/rfcs/index.md` and
   `en/developer/rfcs/index.md`, and a sidebar item under the RFCs group
   (mirror RFC-0001 / RFC-0002).
4. Extend `packages/ai-jue/test/docs-contract.test.ts` locale-pair / sidebar
   assertions when the page is part of the frozen public set.
5. After implementation lands, update Agent profiles and Guide warnings so they
   do not still say Planned / “尚未实现” for shipped Artifact kinds.

A markdown file alone is **not** enough — without the VitePress config entry the
page is orphaned from site navigation (reachable only by direct URL or index
links).

Do not remove existing sidebar entries without updating inbound links and the
docs-contract test.
